# 50-prefix re-baseline — LEG V0: cross_shard_load_sync A/B at the regression point
#
# Decides the core question from the load-gating proposal
# (.dev-context/prefix-routing-load-gating-proposal.md §5, Leg V0): is the +29%
# P99 regression at 13B/10u caused by transient cross-node/cross-shard hot-spotting?
# If enabling cross_shard_load_sync recovers the regression, the fix is a config
# default change — NO new load-gate mechanism is needed.
#
# This file holds the WORKLOAD only (one --compare line). The control variable —
# RANVIER_CROSS_SHARD_LOAD_SYNC — is set in the environment around the runner, so the
# SAME workload runs once with sync OFF and once with sync ON. That knob IS already
# wired into docker-compose.benchmark-real.yml (unlike epsilon/hash_strategy), so no
# compose edit is required for this leg.
#
# Run BOTH arms on the same box, back to back:
#   # V0a — baseline, sync OFF (reproduce the regression here)
#   RANVIER_CROSS_SHARD_LOAD_SYNC=false \
#     ./scripts/bench-runner.sh --suite custom \
#         --file docs/benchmarks/rebaseline/v0-xshard.runs \
#         --repeat 3 --output-dir benchmark-reports/rebaseline/xshard_off
#   # V0b — cross_shard_load_sync ON (100ms default interval; the interval var is
#   #        NOT compose-wired, so the shipped 100ms default applies — which is intended)
#   RANVIER_CROSS_SHARD_LOAD_SYNC=true \
#     ./scripts/bench-runner.sh --suite custom \
#         --file docs/benchmarks/rebaseline/v0-xshard.runs \
#         --repeat 3 --output-dir benchmark-reports/rebaseline/xshard_on
#
# Each line is itself a prefix-vs-round-robin --compare; --repeat 3 writes median/IQR
# aggregates to <output-dir>/aggregates/. Compare V0a's prefix-vs-RR P99 %change against
# V0b's. The RR baseline arm ignores affinity/load, so it is ~invariant to the flag; the
# prefix arm is what moves.
#
# Verdict rule REVISED 2026-09-28, before any V0b run, after V0a measured only +9.7%
# (the original ">=10pp smaller" rule was then unreachable). Recovered: V0b paired median
# P99 change <= 0, verdict not REGRESSION, prefix incompletes <= V0a's 2.3% -> ship sync=true
# as default, no gate. Partial/not recovered -> Leg V1. Full text: load-gating proposal,
# "Amendment 2026-09-28". Capture prometheus_metrics_node*.txt to see active_requests bursts.
#
# Everything rides the CURRENT SHIPPED DEFAULTS (50 prefixes, ratio 0.9, stress, load-aware
# 2.0/floor 2, cache-residency 0.2, 20ms flush, BOUNDED_LOAD). Confirm the "Effective
# Routing Config" banner before trusting any run.

--compare --model meta-llama/CodeLlama-13b-Instruct-hf --warmup --duration 10m --users 10 --max-model-len 8192 --prefix-ratio 0.9 --prompt-dist stress
